# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NON-NEGOTIABLE RULE 7: never commit chart images or dataset content.
# ChartQA is GPL-3.0, RefChartQA is AGPL-3.0. Scripts, IDs, hashes, adapters
# and derived statistics only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two things are load-bearing in these four lines.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash: an unanchored `data/` also matches
# `src/chartqa_dt/data/` — the loaders package — which was silently untracked for nine
# commits while every local test passed and CI failed on ModuleNotFoundError (0050).
#
# `/data/*` and NOT `/data/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so `!/data/MANIFEST.json` under a `/data/` rule is silently a no-op. Excluding
# the directory's *contents* leaves the directory itself visible, which is what makes the
# exceptions work at all. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`, not by reading.
/data/*
!/data/MANIFEST.json
!/data/*.json
!/data/refchartqa_audit.jsonl
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.zip
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.tar
*.tar.gz
!report/figures/*.png
!demo/examples/*.png

# model weights / adapters (pushed to the private HF Hub instead)
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
outputs/
checkpoints/
runs/
wandb/

# credentials
.env
*.key
kaggle.json
.hf_token

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# latex
report/**/*.aux
report/**/*.log
report/**/*.out
report/**/*.toc
report/**/*.bbl
report/**/*.blg
report/**/*.synctex.gz

.kaggle_dataset/
.kaggle_kernel/
outputs/

# LaTeX build products — the PDF is rebuilt from source, never committed
report/**/*.aux
report/**/*.log
report/**/*.out
report/**/*.pdf
report/**/*.toc
report/.DS_Store

# npm deps for the presentation builder — reinstalled with `npm install pptxgenjs`
presentation/node_modules/
presentation/package-lock.json
presentation/package.json
presentation/*.pdf

# Rule 7 ignores *.png so no dataset chart is ever committed. The presentation figures
# are the one safe exception: scripts/make_presentation_figures.py draws them from our
# OWN generated charts, which are this project's work rather than ChartQA (GPL-3.0) or
# RefChartQA (AGPL-3.0) content. Do not widen this to any other path.
!presentation/figures/*.png
